  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0007_4409f40eac3c.png\" style=\"width:1.3806in;height:1.63241in\" /><br />Let <math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5,6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and the point of concurrency of the family&nbsp;of lines&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and foot of the perpendicular from <math><mi>A</mi></math> to the family of lines is <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is perpendicular to <math><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>